  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth in Climate Smart Agribusiness Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Youth in Climate Smart Agribusiness Project aims to empower and engage 400 youths, aged 18-35 in Kano State Nigeria, by the end of 2025. Climate Smart agriculture (CSA) is an integrated approach to managing landscapes &#x2013; croplands, livestock, forests and fisheries, that addresses interlinked challenges of food security and climate change. This initiative will provide comprehensive training in climate-smart agricultural techniques and agribusiness management, targeting youths with diverse background from both rural and urban areas. The project will establish partnerships with local agribusinesses and Flour Mills Nigeria PLC to offer internships and market linkages, ensuring that at least 70% of participants secure employment or start their own agribusiness ventures in wheat farming within six months of completing the program. By fostering an inclusive environment and promoting sustainable practices, the project seeks to enhance food security, stimulate economic growth, and create long-term social and environmental benefits for the broader community.</narrative>
  </description>
